 only on a branch\u002Ftag\u002Fcommit (e.g., a bugfix merged upstream but not yet released), or when you maintain a private fork. Pin to a ",[29,983,984],{},"tag"," for reproducibility, a ",[29,987,988],{},"rev"," for an exact commit, or a ",[29,991,992],{},"branch"," to track evolving work. Avoid ",[29,995,992],{}," in published crates — downstream builds become non-reproducible.",[481,998,999,1002],{},[139,1000,1001],{},"path"," — a local directory. Use during development when you're working on multiple crates simultaneously (e.g., a library + an app that uses it) so changes in one are immediately visible in the other without re-publishing. Path deps are usually paired with a version for when the crate is eventually published.",[481,1004,1005,1008],{},[139,1006,1007],{},"optional"," — a dependency gated behind a feature flag (see below). The dep is only compiled when the feature is enabled, letting you keep heavy\u002Foptional integrations out of the default build.",[19,1010,1011],{"language":644},[23,1012,1014],{"className":647,"code":1013,"language":644,"meta":27,"style":27},"[dependencies]\n# crates.io — the default registry\nserde = \"1.0\"\n\n# git — unpublished, forked, or pre-release\nmy_crate = { git = \"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fuser\u002Fcrate\", branch = \"dev\" }\nmy_crate2 = { git = \"...\", tag = \"v1.2.3\" }     # reproducible\nmy_crate3 = { git = \"...\", rev = \"abc123\" }     # exact commit\n\n# path — local monorepo development\nmy_local = { path = \"..\u002Fmy_local\" }\n\n# optional — only compiled if the \"extra\" feature is enabled\nextra = { version = \"1.0\", optional = true }\n",[29,1015,1016,1024,1029,1037,1041,1046,1063,1083,1101,1105,1110,1120,1124,1129],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1017,1018,1020,1022],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1019,655],{"class":53},[32,1021,746],{"class":49},[32,1023,661],{"class":53},[32,1025,1026],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1027,1028],{"class":38},"# crates.io — the default registry\n",[32,1030,1031,1034],{"class":34,"line":57},[32,1032,1033],{"class":53},"serde = ",[32,1035,1036],{"class":66},"\"1.0\"\n",[32,1038,1039],{"class":34,"line":73},[32,1040,739],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":738},[32,1042,1043],{"class":34,"line":214},[32,1044,1045],{"class":38},"# git — unpublished, forked, or pre-release\n",[32,1047,1048,1051,1054,1057,1060],{"class":34,"line":239},[32,1049,1050],{"class":53},"my_crate = { git = ",[32,1052,1053],{"class":66},"\"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fuser\u002Fcrate\"",[32,1055,1056],{"class":53},", branch = ",[32,1058,1059],{"class":66},"\"dev\"",[32,1061,1062],{"class":53}," }\n",[32,1064,1065,1068,1071,1074,1077,1080],{"class":34,"line":255},[32,1066,1067],{"class":53},"my_crate2 = { git = ",[32,1069,1070],{"class":66},"\"...\"",[32,1072,1073],{"class":53},", tag = ",[32,1075,1076],{"class":66},"\"v1.2.3\"",[32,1078,1079],{"class":53}," }     ",[32,1081,1082],{"class":38},"# reproducible\n",[32,1084,1085,1088,1090,1093,1096,1098],{"class":34,"line":270},[32,1086,1087],{"class":53},"my_crate3 = { git = ",[32,1089,1070],{"class":66},[32,1091,1092],{"class":53},", rev = ",[32,1094,1095],{"class":66},"\"abc123\"",[32,1097,1079],{"class":53},[32,1099,1100],{"class":38},"# exact commit\n",[32,1102,1103],{"class":34,"line":286},[32,1104,739],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":738},[32,1106,1107],{"class":34,"line":310},[32,1108,1109],{"class":38},"# path — local monorepo development\n",[32,1111,1112,1115,1118],{"class":34,"line":333},[32,1113,1114],{"class":53},"my_local = { path = ",[32,1116,1117],{"class":66},"\"..\u002Fmy_local\"",[32,1119,1062],{"class":53},[32,1121,1122],{"class":34,"line":357},[32,1123,739],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":738},[32,1125,1126],{"class":34,"line":373},[32,1127,1128],{"class":38},"# optional — only compiled if the \"extra\" feature is enabled\n",[32,1130,1131,1134,1136,1139,1142],{"class":34,"line":783},[32,1132,1133],{"class":53},"extra = { version = ",[32,1135,756],{"class":66},[32,1137,1138],{"class":53},", optional = ",[32,1140,1141],{"class":178},"true",[32,1143,1062],{"class":53},[14,1145,1146],{"id":887},"Features",[393,1148,1150],{"id":1149},"why-features-exist","Why features exist",[78,1152,1153,1154,1157,1158,1161,1162,1164,1165,1168,1169,1172],{},"A feature is a ",[139,1155,1156],{},"compile-time switch"," that conditionally includes code, dependencies, or modules. They exist so a single crate can serve multiple use cases without forcing every user to compile everything — e.g., a HTTP client that's async-only behind a ",[29,1159,1160],{},"\"async\""," feature, or a serializer with optional ",[29,1163,898],{},"\u002F",[29,1166,1167],{},"\"yaml\""," backends. Code gated by ",[29,1170,1171],{},"#[cfg(feature = \"...\")]"," is only compiled when the feature is on.",[78,1174,1175,1176,1179,1180,1184,1185,1188,1189,1192,1193,1195],{},"The important mechanic to understand is ",[139,1177,1178],{},"feature unification",": if ",[1181,1182,1183],"em",{},"any"," crate in your dependency graph enables a feature, it's enabled for ",[1181,1186,1187],{},"all"," uses of that crate in the build. This is why exposing features of your dependencies to your users is risky — your library's ",[29,1190,1191],{},"serde"," feature and a downstream crate's ",[29,1194,1191],{}," feature unify, and you may end up with features you didn't ask for. The safe pattern is to use direct dependencies + optional features rather than re-exporting a dependency's features.",[19,1197,1198],{"language":21},[23,1199,1201],{"className":25,"code":1200,"language":21,"meta":27,"style":27},"#[cfg(feature = \"json\")]\nmod json;          \u002F\u002F only compiled when the \"json\" feature is enabled\n",[29,1202,1203,1216],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1204,1205,1208,1210,1213],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1206,1207],{"class":53},"#[cfg(feature ",[32,1209,160],{"class":45},[32,1211,1212],{"class":66}," \"json\"",[32,1214,1215],{"class":53},")]\n",[32,1217,1218,1221,1224,1227],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1219,1220],{"class":45},"mod",[32,1222,1223],{"class":49}," json",[32,1225,1226],{"class":53},";          ",[32,1228,1229],{"class":38},"\u002F\u002F only compiled when the \"json\" feature is enabled\n",[393,1231,1233],{"id":1232},"when-to-define-your-own-features","When to define your own features",[78,1235,1236,1237,1240,1241,1244],{},"Define a feature when you want users to opt into functionality that has a compile-time or runtime cost (a heavy dependency, an async runtime, a CLI mode). Keep features ",[139,1238,1239],{},"additive"," (they only turn things ",[1181,1242,1243],{},"on",", never off) so unification can never break a downstream build.",[14,1246,1248],{"id":1247},"cargolock",[29,1249,1250],{},"Cargo.lock",[478,1252,1253,1256,1267],{},[481,1254,1255],{},"Pin exact versions resolved for your dependency graph.",[481,1257,1258,1259,1262,1263,1266],{},"Always commit for ",[139,1260,1261],{},"binaries",". For ",[139,1264,1265],{},"libraries"," the official recommendation is also to commit it, but it's commonly gitignored.",[481,1268,1269,1272,1273,1276],{},[29,1270,1271],{},"cargo update"," bumps within semver-compatible range; ",[29,1274,1275],{},"cargo update -p serde --precise 1.0.150"," pins a single crate.",[14,1278,1280],{"id":1279},"workspaces","Workspaces",[393,1282,1284],{"id":1283},"why-workspaces-exist","Why workspaces exist",[78,1286,1287,1288,1291,1292,1294,1295,1297,1298,1301,1302,1305],{},"A workspace lets multiple crates share a single ",[29,1289,1290],{},"target\u002F"," directory, a single ",[29,1293,1250],{},", and a unified set of dependency versions. Without a workspace, each crate in a monorepo would have its own ",[29,1296,1290],{}," (disk + compile-time waste), its own lockfile (drifting dependency versions across crates), and its own resolution (one crate could pull ",[29,1299,1300],{},"serde 1.0.150"," while another pulls ",[29,1303,1304],{},"serde 1.0.180","). The workspace makes them one build graph.",[393,1307,1309],{"id":1308},"when-to-use-a-workspace","When to use a workspace",[78,1311,1312,1313,1316,1317,1320,1321,1320,1324,1327],{},"Reach for a workspace when you have ",[139,1314,1315],{},"multiple related crates"," that you want to evolve together: a multi-crate library (e.g., ",[29,1318,1319],{},"core"," + ",[29,1322,1323],{},"derive",[29,1325,1326],{},"macros","), a monorepo with an app + shared internal libraries, or a project with separate binary + library + tooling crates. Keep a single crate if there's only one publishable unit — a workspace adds structure you don't need.",[78,1329,1330,1331,1334,1335,1338],{},"The ",[29,1332,1333],{},"[workspace.dependencies]"," table lets you declare a dependency version once and have every member crate reference it via ",[29,1336,1337],{},"crate.workspace = true",", so versions stay unified without copy-pasting.",[19,1340,1341],{"language":644},[23,1342,1344],{"className":647,"code":1343,"language":644,"meta":27,"style":27},"# Cargo.toml (workspace root)\n[workspace]\nmembers = [\"crates\u002F*\", \"app\"]\n\n[workspace.dependencies]\nserde = \"1.0\"\n",[29,1345,1346,1351,1360,1375,1379,1392],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1347,1348],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1349,1350],{"class":38},"# Cargo.toml (workspace root)\n",[32,1352,1353,1355,1358],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1354,655],{"class":53},[32,1356,1357],{"class":49},"workspace",[32,1359,661],{"class":53},[32,1361,1362,1365,1368,1370,1373],{"class":34,"line":57},[32,1363,1364],{"class":53},"members = [",[32,1366,1367],{"class":66},"\"crates\u002F*\"",[32,1369,296],{"class":53},[32,1371,1372],{"class":66},"\"app\"",[32,1374,661],{"class":53},[32,1376,1377],{"class":34,"line":73},[32,1378,739],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":738},[32,1380,1381,1383,1385,1388,1390],{"class":34,"line":214},[32,1382,655],{"class":53},[32,1384,1357],{"class":49},[32,1386,1387],{"class":53},".",[32,1389,746],{"class":49},[32,1391,661],{"class":53},[32,1393,1394,1396],{"class":34,"line":239},[32,1395,1033],{"class":53},[32,1397,1036],{"class":66},[78,1399,1400,1401,1387],{},"Members then reference with ",[29,1402,1403],{},"serde.workspace = true",[14,1405,1407],{"id":1406},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[478,1409,1410,1419,1439,1455,1474,1487],{},[481,1411,1412,1414,1415,1418],{},[139,1413,413],{},": ",[29,1416,1417],{},"rustc --explain E0382"," (or any error code from a compiler message) prints a detailed explanation with examples, straight from the compiler — faster than searching online for a common error code.",[481,1420,1421,1424,1425,1428,1429,1432,1433,1435,1436,1438],{},[139,1422,1423],{},"Idiom",": use ",[29,1426,1427],{},"println!(\"{name:?}\")"," (Debug) while prototyping and switch to ",[29,1430,1431],{},"println!(\"{name}\")"," (Display) once a type has a hand-written ",[29,1434,405],{}," impl — reaching for ",[29,1437,409],{}," everywhere works but produces developer-facing, not user-facing, output.",[481,1440,1441,1443,1444,1447,1448,1450,1451,1454],{},[139,1442,1423],{},": set ",[29,1445,1446],{},"publish = false"," in ",[29,1449,640],{}," immediately for any project that isn't meant for crates.io — it costs nothing and prevents an accidental ",[29,1452,1453],{},"cargo publish"," months later when you've forgotten the project was never meant to be public.",[481,1456,1457,1414,1459,1462,1463,1466,1467,1470,1471,1473],{},[139,1458,413],{},[29,1460,1461],{},"cargo run -- --flag value"," — everything after the bare ",[29,1464,1465],{},"--"," is passed to ",[1181,1468,1469],{},"your"," binary's argv, not interpreted by Cargo; forgetting the ",[29,1472,1465],{}," is a common reason \"my CLI flag doesn't work\" during local testing.",[481,1475,1476,1478,1479,1482,1483,1486],{},[139,1477,1423],{},": pin dependencies with ",[29,1480,1481],{},"\"=\""," only when you have a specific reason (a known-broken later version, reproducibility requirements) — the default caret (",[29,1484,1485],{},"^",") requirement is usually right, since it allows patch\u002Fminor updates that are supposed to be backward compatible under semver.",[481,1488,1489,1414,1492,1495,1496,1498,1499,1502,1503,296,1506,296,1509,1512],{},[139,1490,1491],{},"Performance",[29,1493,1494],{},"cargo new","'s default ",[29,1497,640],{}," doesn't set a release profile — for anything beyond a quick script, add ",[29,1500,1501],{},"[profile.release]"," tuning (",[29,1504,1505],{},"lto",[29,1507,1508],{},"codegen-units",[29,1510,1511],{},"strip",") once you're past the prototyping stage, since the untouched defaults favor compile speed over runtime performance.",[14,1514,1516],{"id":1515},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[478,1518,1519,1539,1556,1574,1588,1597],{},[481,1520,1521,1527,1528,1531,1532,1535,1536,1387],{},[139,1522,1523,1524],{},"Binaries from ",[29,1525,1526],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F*.rs",": each ",[29,1529,1530],{},".rs"," file in ",[29,1533,1534],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F"," becomes a separate binary target automatically. Run with ",[29,1537,1538],{},"cargo run --bin extra",[481,1540,1541,1414,1549,1552,1553,1387],{},[139,1542,1543,1546,1547],{},[29,1544,1545],{},"cargo run"," passes args after ",[29,1548,1465],{},[29,1550,1551],{},"cargo run -- --flag"," runs your binary with ",[29,1554,1555],{},"--flag",[481,1557,1558,1565,1566,1569,1570,1573],{},[139,1559,1560,1561,1564],{},"Multiple ",[29,1562,1563],{},"[[bin]]"," targets"," can share a ",[29,1567,1568],{},"src\u002Flib.rs"," for logic and have thin ",[29,1571,1572],{},"src\u002Fbin\u002F*"," shells.",[481,1575,1576,1414,1581,1584,1585,1587],{},[139,1577,1578,1580],{},[29,1579,83],{}," error codes",[29,1582,1583],{},"E0382"," etc. Search ",[29,1586,1417],{}," or online for detailed explanations.",[481,1589,1590,1414,1593,1596],{},[139,1591,1592],{},"Build scripts",[29,1594,1595],{},"build.rs"," runs before compilation; use for linking C libs, generating code at build time.",[481,1598,1599,1414,1605,296,1608,1611,1612,1387],{},[139,1600,1601,1604],{},[29,1602,1603],{},"CARGO_*"," env vars",[29,1606,1607],{},"CARGO_PKG_VERSION",[29,1609,1610],{},"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR",", etc., useful in build scripts and via ",[29,1613,1614],{},"env!",[14,1616,1618],{"id":1617},"reading-compiler-errors","Reading Compiler Errors",[78,1620,1621,1622,1625],{},"Rust errors are structured: the message, an ",[29,1623,1624],{},"-->"," pointing at the code, and often a help\u002Fnote. Multi-error cascades are common — fix the first error, then re-run; later ones often vanish.",[14,1627,1629],{"id":1628},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[78,1631,1632,1633,1636],{},"Why does ",[29,1634,1635],{},"cargo build"," succeed for one teammate and fail with a totally different error for another, on the exact same commit?",[19,1638,1639],{"language":644},[23,1640,1642],{"className":647,"code":1641,"language":644,"meta":27,"style":27},"[dependencies]\nsome_lib = \"1.2\"\n",[29,1643,1644,1652],{"__ignoreMap":27},[32,1645,1646,1648,1650],{"class":34,"line":35},[32,1647,655],{"class":53},[32,1649,746],{"class":49},[32,1651,661],{"class":53},[32,1653,1654,1657],{"class":34,"line":42},[32,1655,1656],{"class":53},"some_lib = ",[32,1658,1659],{"class":66},"\"1.2\"\n",[1661,1662,1663,1667,1713,1719],"details",{},[1664,1665,1666],"summary",{},"Answer",[78,1668,1669,1670,1672,1673,1676,1677,1680,1681,1683,1684,1686,1687,1690,1691,1694,1695,1698,1699,1702,1703,1706,1707,1709,1710,1712],{},"The most common cause: one teammate has a ",[29,1671,1250],{}," committed and checked out (or previously generated) that pins ",[29,1674,1675],{},"some_lib"," to, say, ",[29,1678,1679],{},"1.2.3",", while the other teammate either deleted their ",[29,1682,1250],{},", is building a fresh checkout without one, or ran ",[29,1685,1271],{}," locally — resolving ",[29,1688,1689],{},"\"1.2\""," (which means ",[29,1692,1693],{},"^1.2",", i.e., ",[29,1696,1697],{},">=1.2.0, \u003C2.0.0",") to a newer version like ",[29,1700,1701],{},"1.5.0"," that was published after the first teammate last locked their dependencies. Cargo.toml's version requirement is a ",[1181,1704,1705],{},"range",", not a pin — the actual, exact version used for any given build is determined by ",[29,1708,1250],{},", and if that file is missing, out of date, or excluded from version control, two people (or two CI runs, or a local build vs. a Docker build) can silently resolve to different concrete versions of ",[29,1711,1675],{},", one of which may have introduced a breaking change or bug despite being \"semver compatible\" in theory.",[78,1714,1715,1716,1718],{},"This is precisely why the chapter's guidance is to always commit ",[29,1717,1250],{}," for binaries (and, per current official guidance, for libraries too): it's the only thing that guarantees everyone — teammates, CI, and production builds — resolves the exact same dependency graph.",[78,1720,1721,1414,1724,1726,1727,1729,1730,1732,1733,1736],{},[139,1722,1723],{},"The lesson",[29,1725,640],{}," version requirements describe an acceptable ",[1181,1728,1705],{},"; only ",[29,1731,1250],{}," pins the ",[1181,1734,1735],{},"exact"," versions actually used — an uncommitted or stale lock file means \"works on my machine\" can be literally true and still not mean what you think it means.",[14,1738,1739],{"id":1664},"Summary",[78,1741,1742],{},"You can scaffold, build, run, format, lint, and document a project. Next: the type system starts with variables and mutability.",[1744,1745,1746],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decorati